course: dictionary
lesson: 7496
title: Words for where we live
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words are easy to work out from the words around them. «You learn your postcode or ZIP code, because it helps letters to be delivered quickly.» The sentence says the code helps letters arrive quickly, so a postcode is a code that helps post reach the right place.
explain: Look at the first sentence: «An address goes in this order: the name, then house number and street, then town or city, then state or county, then postcode or ZIP code.» The postcode comes last, at the end of the address. That is the clue that it is added to the end.
explain: The word can also name a small area. Everyone who shares the same postcode lives in the same local place. Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence: «In an emergency the most important thing is to tell the services where you are, so children should learn their full address and postcode.» Does the meaning still make sense? It does.
explain: Different countries use different names for the same job. In the USA it is a «ZIP code», in Canada a «postal code», and in Ireland the «Eircode». The job is the same: helping post get delivered to the right place.
fact: A postcode is a group of letters and numbers added to the end of an address.
fact: It helps the post get delivered to the right place quickly.
fact: In the UK a postcode looks like «SW1A 1AA», while in Australia and New Zealand it is four numbers.
fact: A postcode also names the small area that shares it.
fact: Keep your address and postcode private online, but know them in case you need help.
exercise: What is a postcode? | A message from the postman | A picture of a house on a card | A type of stamp | *A group of letters and numbers added to the end of an address
exercise: In the USA, what is a postcode called? | *ZIP code | Postal van | Eircode | Post box
exercise: «You learn your postcode or ZIP code, because it helps letters to be delivered quickly.» Why do we learn it? | It makes the letter a different colour | *It helps letters to be delivered quickly | It is a secret password | It tells the time of the post
test: «In an emergency the most important thing is to tell the services where you are, so children should learn their full address and postcode.» What does knowing your postcode help with? | Counting coins | Drawing a map of the moon | Choosing a birthday present | *Telling the services where you are
test: Which order is correct for an address? | *Name, house number and street, town or city, then postcode | Street, postcode, name, town | Postcode, name, house number and street, town | Town, then postcode, then name, then street
exam: Besides the code itself, what else can a postcode name? | A type of post box | A kind of stamp | A delivery van | *A small area that shares the same postcode
